  "arguments": {
    "purpose": "Classify each reverse-engineering area of the Ford Racing 2 PS2 corpus by evidence status for a completion matrix",
    "context": "Corpus: unchanged PAL SLES-517.05. Claims are limited to measured structure; semantics need separate evidence. User constraints: no debugger windows or focus stealing; milestone #2 evidence is bounded and issue #2 lists audio codec, mesh, full PTG and UI/text as separate investigations.",
    "classes": [
      {
        "id": "verified_behavior",
        "description": "A behavior or fact checked against real observations or independent bytes/oracle on the real corpus, with a passing executable check and no known counterexample. Example: archive output SHA-256 equals independent extraction. Takes precedence over supported_bounded_profile only if the claim is about an observed behavior rather than a structural rule."
      },
      {
        "id": "supported_bounded_profile",
        "description": "A structural rule or contract verified on the exact corpus profile with negative tests, whose claims are explicitly limited (no semantics, no other regions). Example: header relations hold on all 548 PTG files. Use when the rule is structural and bounded, even if semantics are unknown."
      },
      {
        "id": "unresolved_interpretation",
        "description": "The data exists and is measured, but its meaning is not established; competing or no hypotheses survived testing. Example: palette location for tiled PTG files. Beats missing_observation when bytes are available and only meaning is missing."
      },
      {
        "id": "missing_observation",
        "description": "Establishing the fact needs a runtime or hardware observation that has not been made (e.g., a capture of a specific event). Beats missing_prerequisite when the only blocker is making the observation itself with tools already present."
      },
      {
        "id": "missing_prerequisite",
        "description": "Work is blocked by an absent tool, input, authorization or user decision that is not yet available (e.g., a windowless emulator mode, a native decompiler, a hardware oracle, or the user's scope decision)."
      },
      {
        "id": "not_yet_probed",
        "description": "No measurement has been made at all; neither structure nor meaning is known beyond file counts."
      },
      {
        "id": "manual_review",
        "description": "Genuinely ambiguous between classes; needs a human or independent reasoner."
      }
    ],
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "archive_container",
        "text": "HDR/DAT archive: 48 segments, 1037 records, 990 files (604 zlib, 386 raw); every output length and SHA-256 equals an independent extraction; verified against two real runtime loads."
      },
      {
        "id": "static_loader",
        "text": "R5900 loader stages (init, lookup, chunk read, raw transfer, decompression, consumption) mapped to instruction bytes in a complete 3446-function Ghidra export; no native decompiler, so no recovered C."
      },
      {
        "id": "runtime_loads",
        "text": "Two real PCSX2 loading events (one raw, one zlib), each repeated, outputs equal independent extraction; only two assets observed; capture opens debugger windows."
      },
      {
        "id": "bank_structure",
        "text": "27 sound-bank pairs: descriptor chains exact; all 305 sample spans obey PS-ADPCM block structure; reference decoder matches ffmpeg on all 305 spans exactly."
      },
      {
        "id": "bank_hardware_playback",
        "text": "Whether the decoded bank audio is bit-exact with SPU2 hardware and how the game uploads/plays it; no hardware oracle, no observed upload."
      },
      {
        "id": "music_streams",
        "text": "20 .mib/.mih music streams: 2-channel 0x8000 interleave, mih word 5 equals turn count, ADPCM structure holds, 40 excerpts match ffmpeg; mih word 1 meaning and loop behavior unknown, no loop flags present."
      },
      {
        "id": "model_name_tree",
        "text": "56 .ps2 model name trees end exactly at the string pool; leading u32 equals the name-pool end offset in 56/56; zero pad to 16-byte boundary."
      },
      {
        "id": "model_geometry",
        "text": "Geometry after the name pool is only hashed; the later header words are not stable across files; 16-bit index runs seen but no layout hypothesis tested."
      },
      {
        "id": "ptg_gear_sprites",
        "text": "Eight gear sprites plus 8 more count==1 files decode with the supported sprite profile; uppercase R and N confirmed by the user; pixel hashes are regressions."
      },
      {
        "id": "ptg_header_relations",
        "text": "All 548 PTG headers obey count == columns*rows, stride == cell, columns/rows == ceil(dimension/cell); 0 violations."
      },
      {
        "id": "ptg_tiled_dd",
        "text": "17 files with 0xDDDDDDDD last word follow exact size 1120+1104*count, row-major tile extent floats, constant descriptors; palette, pointer values and descriptor constants unresolved; raw indices render a recognizable logo."
      },
      {
        "id": "ptg_header_only",
        "text": "491 multi-tile PTG files outside the measured profile are checked at header level only; body layout unknown."
      },
      {
        "id": "ui_text_cfg",
        "text": "216 .dat, 45 .ui, 16 .cfg, 5 .mbf files; text-like per earlier notes, no measurement or grammar recovered."
      },
      {
        "id": "ee_iop_vu_consumers",
        "text": "What EE, IOP and VU code does with loaded sound, texture and model buffers; 3446 functions inventoried but consumers unmapped; IOP module set (IOPRP255.IMG) not enumerated."
      },
      {
        "id": "fresh_windowless_capture",
        "text": "A fresh PCSX2 capture mode that opens no windows and takes no focus; the current path opens debugger windows and the user forbade repeating that."
      },
      {
        "id": "broader_finish_line",
        "text": "Whether the overall effort should end at bounded asset-format evidence or extend to mesh, VU and render reconstruction or whole-game decompilation; the user's explicit mandate is not established."
      }
    ]
  },
